$WW,1$$FG,5,1$ZealOS Virtual File System (VFS)$FG$$LK,"POSIX Compatibility Layer",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/README.DD"$

$FG,2$Overview$FG$

The VFS layer provides a unified interface for multiple filesystem types,
enabling ZealOS to access various storage formats beyond the native RedSea
filesystem.

$FG,2$Components$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,3$Core VFS ($LK,"VFS.HH",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/VFS.HH"$ / $LK,"VFS.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/VFS.ZC"$)$FG$
  - Unified filesystem interface
  - Inode caching
  - Directory entry (dentry) caching
  - Path resolution with symlink following
  - Mount point management

$FG,3$Symbolic Links ($LK,"Symlink.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/Symlink.ZC"$)$FG$
  - Overlay symlink table for native filesystems
  - Persistent symlink database (/Home/POSIX/etc/symlinks.db)
  - POSIX-compatible API (symlink, readlink, lstat, realpath)

$FG,3$Ext2/3/4 Driver ($LK,"ext4/Ext4.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/ext4/Ext4.ZC"$)$FG$
  - Support for Ext2, Ext3, and Ext4 filesystems
  - Extent-based and indirect block mapping
  - 64-bit block addressing
  - Read-only for safety
  - BSD-2-Clause licensed (based on FreeBSD concepts)

$FG,3$NTFS Driver ($LK,"ntfs/NTFS.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/ntfs/NTFS.ZC"$)$FG$
  - Read-only access to NTFS volumes
  - MFT record parsing
  - Run list decoding
  - UTF-16 to UTF-8 filename conversion
  - MIT licensed (clean-room implementation)

$FG,3$FUSE Interface ($LK,"fuse/FUSE.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/fuse/FUSE.ZC"$)$FG$
  - FUSE-compatible API for user-space filesystems
  - Implement filesystems in HolyC
  - Full read/write support
  - MIT licensed
$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Usage$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,3$Loading All Filesystem Support$FG$
  #include "/Home/POSIX/vfs/MakeAllFS.ZC"

$FG,3$Mounting an Ext4 Filesystem$FG$
  VFSMount("/dev/sda1", "/mnt/linux", "ext4", 0, NULL);

$FG,3$Mounting an NTFS Volume$FG$
  VFSMount("/dev/sdb1", "/mnt/windows", "ntfs", 0, NULL);

$FG,3$Creating a FUSE Filesystem$FG$
  See $LK,"Examples/HelloFS.ZC",A="FI:/Home/POSIX/vfs/fuse/Examples/HelloFS.ZC"$
$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Architecture$FG$

$ID,2$
  +-------------------+
  |  User Application |
  +-------------------+
           |
           v
  +-------------------+
  |    POSIX libc     |
  |  (unistd.h, etc)  |
  +-------------------+
           |
           v
  +-------------------+
  |       VFS         |
  |  - Path resolution|
  |  - Inode cache    |
  |  - Mount points   |
  +-------------------+
           |
     +-----+-----+-----+
     |     |     |     |
     v     v     v     v
  +----+ +----+ +----+ +----+
  |ext4| |ntfs| |fuse| |... |
  +----+ +----+ +----+ +----+
           |
           v
  +-------------------+
  |   Block Device    |
  +-------------------+
$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Filesystem Operations$FG$

$ID,2$$FG,3$Superblock Operations$FG$
  - mount    - Mount a filesystem
  - unmount  - Unmount a filesystem
  - sync     - Synchronize filesystem
  - statfs   - Get filesystem statistics

$FG,3$Inode Operations$FG$
  - lookup   - Look up name in directory
  - create   - Create file
  - mkdir    - Create directory
  - rmdir    - Remove directory
  - unlink   - Remove file
  - rename   - Rename file/directory
  - link     - Create hard link
  - symlink  - Create symbolic link
  - readlink - Read symbolic link target
  - getattr  - Get file attributes
  - setattr  - Set file attributes
  - truncate - Change file size

$FG,3$File Operations$FG$
  - open     - Open file
  - close    - Close file
  - read     - Read data
  - write    - Write data
  - readdir  - Read directory entries
  - seek     - Change file position
  - fsync    - Synchronize file
  - ioctl    - Device control
$ID,-2$

$FG,2$Licenses$FG$

$ID,2$- VFS Core: MIT
- Symlink Support: MIT
- Ext4 Driver: BSD-2-Clause (FreeBSD-derived)
- NTFS Driver: MIT (clean-room)
- FUSE Interface: MIT$ID,-2$

